<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/014Y">Example <span data-tag="014Y">4.2.4.6</span>.</a> The inclusion map $i_0: \{ 0\}  \hookrightarrow \Delta ^1$ is left anodyne (and therefore anodyne). However, it is not right anodyne (and therefore not inner anodyne). This follows from Proposition <a data-tag="014X" href="/tag/014X">4.2.4.5</a>, since the lifting problem </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \{ 0\}  \ar [r]^-{\operatorname{id}} \ar [d]^{i_0} &amp;  \{ 0\}  \ar [d]^{i_0} \\ \Delta ^1 \ar [r]^-{\operatorname{id}} \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur] &amp;  \Delta ^1 } \]
</div>
<p> does not admit a solution (note that the inclusion map $i_0: \{ 0\}  \hookrightarrow \Delta ^1$ is a right fibration; see Warning <a data-tag="00TD" href="/tag/00TD">4.2.1.6</a>). </p>
</article>
